  "abstract": "Covers the IETF WIMSE (Workload Identity in Multi-System Environments) working group drafts for service-to-service authentication: the architecture (draft-ietf-wimse-arch-08), the Workload Identifier and wimse URI scheme (identifier-03), the Workload Identity Token and Workload Identity Certificate (workload-creds-02), the Workload Proof Token (wpt-02), the RFC 9421 HTTP Message Signatures profile (http-signature-07), mutual TLS (mutual-tls-02), Workload Identity Practices (workload-identity-practices-07, with the IESG) and the AI Identity Management System (aims-00). None is an RFC. Each draft is its own version family whose current line is its latest revision with a draft posture; the replaced draft-ietf-wimse-s2s-protocol-07, the Workload-Proof-Token header of wpt-01 and the @request-target profile of http-signature-06 are legacy lines with upgrade checklists. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, architecture and identifiers, WIT and WPT, HTTP signatures and mTLS, and practices with AIMS, and relate each to SPIFFE and OAuth.",
